  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>asparaginase</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L01XX02</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, IV dosing <small>(PK_2C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Borghorst S et al. 2012</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>pediatric patients with previously untreated acute lymphoblastic leukemia</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>asparaginase</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_asparaginase/Asparaginase_Borghorst2012_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>total body clearance</td><td>0.13</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume of distribution in the central compartment</td><td>4.11</td><td>L</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume of distribution in the peripheral compartment</td><td>1.63</td><td>L</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr><tr><td>intercompartmental clearance</td><td>0.106</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr></table><h4>About asparaginase</h4><p>Asparaginase is an enzyme medication used as an anticancer drug to treat lymphoma and lymphoid leukemia. It is an approved medicine, included on the WHO list of essential medicines, and is authorised in the European Union for precursor cell lymphoblastic leukemia-lymphoma.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q105296036\">Wikidata Q105296036</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Asparaginase\">Asparaginase</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Borghorst S et al. (2012). Population pharmacokinetics of native Escherichia coli asparaginase. <i>Pediatric hematology and oncology 29(2):154–165</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3109/08880018.2011.627978\">10.3109/08880018.2011.627978</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22376019\">22376019</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Borghorst_2012: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
